# Valley Floodcaller: "You may cast noncreature spells as though they had flash" (CR 307.5, 702.8). Embereth
# Shieldbreaker is a creature card, but cast as its Adventure it is only Battle Display, a sorcery (CR 715.3a: only the
# Adventure's characteristics are judged), so in Bot2's second main phase Bot1 casts Battle Display on Bot2's
# Ornithopter. Just before, the card cast as the creature is refused (`Ability: #1`, the cast for its mana cost) with
# the mana for it at hand; after Battle Display resolves, the creature on its adventure is refused from exile too, and is
# cast from there in Bot1's own main phase (CR 715.4), the positive control at sorcery timing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Valley Floodcaller
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Embereth Shieldbreaker
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Valley Floodcaller.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main2]
! Bot1.Hand.Embereth Shieldbreaker.Cast(Ability: #1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Embereth Shieldbreaker.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter; Ability: Adventure)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Exile.Embereth Shieldbreaker.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Exile.Embereth Shieldbreaker.Cast

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Embereth Shieldbreaker.Power = 2
Exile.Count = 0
